{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Janitor Phase 4: RP10 approved as refined on 2026-08-30 after maintained-OSS comparison. Approved scope: one pure Jira-family canonicalizer owns raw `issuelinks` parsing, inward/outward direction, malformed or unmapped fallback, deduplication, and canonical link-observation construction; Jira Cloud and Data Center keep separate transports and delegate to it; shared behavior vectors exercise both delegates. The provider-neutral core retains the canonical relation contract and desired-vs-observed diff. Redesigning the still Jira-shaped `SupportsLinks` protocol is explicitly outside RP10."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788125671828548279,"uuid":"33c2e124-1c84-4180-b4eb-c6ef9ef3e5ab"}